Petrology — Dexter Perkins, open textbook (@mp-petrology: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_6P7JBVJJ3P1BT6QKDGC7BN6VWV
Dexter Perkins. Petrology. University of North Dakota, repository citation 2022; the deposited ebook is described as current through April 2023. DOI 10.31356/oers030. [Authorized ebook, PDF, and citation](https://commons.und.edu/oers/30/) · [Maintained author edition](https://opengeology.org/petrology/).

Read the complete book as a sustained petrological companion, using its actual contents and edition for the assigned rock/process topics. Combine it with the complete igneous, metamorphic, and sedimentary course sequences, so a textbook title does not stand in for the methods and practical work.

The repository states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Preserve original and component notices. The catalogue, revision description, citation, and authorized formats were checked on 29 October 2026. A direct PDF request returned 403 and the live host presented a browser challenge; these limits are not represented as full inspection of every page. No ebook, PDF, or media is bundled.

